---
// "Worth the visit?" — a vote, and beside it a separate way to report a problem.
//
// Split apart 2026-08-16 on Hidde's instruction: "je kunt een boom niet leuk
// vinden of niet de moeite vinden zonder dat er iets mis is." The first version
// (his own design of 2026-08-14) hung four chips off the thumbs-down under the
// heading "What was wrong?", and one of those chips was "Not that special",
// which is an opinion rather than a fault. So the control asked everyone who
// simply was not impressed to file a fault report, and gave everyone who loved
// the tree but found the pin wrong no way in at all.
//
// The convention, checked against the standing references before rebuilding:
// Google Maps keeps its rating and its "Suggest an edit" as two separate entry
// points; AllTrails separates the star rating from reporting conditions;
// YouTube and Reddit separate the vote from Report. Everywhere, opinion and
// error report are siblings, never nested. Nesting hides the report from the
// people most likely to have one and interrogates the people least likely.
//
// THE SAME CONTROL AS THE APP, since 2026-09-11 (Hidde: "zorg dat deze pagina
// gelijk wordt getrokken met de app die is goed"). On 2026-09-04 he moved the
// app's thumb up beside the place name and took the question away ("de worth
// the visit tekst mag helemaal weg, zet die thumb omhoog gewoon naast de
// stadsnaam"), put "Something's wrong" low on the page, and the app had
// already dropped the thumbs-down. The website kept all of it for a week. So
// the two halves now render in two places, chosen with `part`:
//
//   part="vote"    one thumb, inline beside the place, nothing else. The
//                  pressed state IS the confirmation, which is what the script
//                  already said; "Thanks, counted" is gone with it.
//   part="report"  "Something's wrong" and its chips, low on the page.
//   (no part)      both, for any page that has no place line to sit in.
//
// There is no thumbs-down on either surface. "Not worth it" is what a missing
// thumb already says, and the fault chips carry every reason that is a fault.
//
// Where a report goes is unchanged: the same Supabase submissions table the
// /contribute form uses (kind 'feedback'), where Step 0b picks it up, and a
// dead or wrong-location report gets checked the same day.
//
// Both halves carry the tree on their own box, because worthit-js.ts scopes
// everything to the nearest `.worthit` and reads the tree from it; the vote
// state is shared per tree, so the two boxes never disagree.
interface Props {
  treeId: string;
  city: string;
  treeName: string;
  compact?: boolean;
  part?: "vote" | "report";
}
const { treeId, city, treeName, compact = false, part } = Astro.props;
const showVote = part !== "report";
const showReport = part !== "vote";
const cls = ["worthit", compact ? "worthit-compact" : "", part === "vote" ? "worthit-inline" : ""].filter(Boolean).join(" ");
---
<div class={cls} data-tree={treeId} data-city={city} data-name={treeName}>
  <div class="worthit-row">
    {showVote && (
      <button type="button" class="worthit-btn" data-vote="up" aria-label={`Yes, ${treeName} was worth the visit`}>👍</button>
    )}
    {showReport && (
      <button type="button" class="worthit-report" aria-expanded="false">Something's wrong</button>
    )}
  </div>
  {showReport && (
    <Fragment>
      <div class="worthit-why" hidden>
        <span class="worthit-q">What's wrong?</span>
        <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="dead or gone" data-q="What did you find there? (optional)" data-ph="A stump, a fallen trunk, nothing at all, and when you were there">It's dead or gone</button>
        <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="wrong location" data-q="Where is it really? (optional)" data-ph="A street corner, a landmark, or paste a maps pin">Wrong location</button>
        <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="could not tell which tree" data-q="Which one did you look at? (optional)" data-ph="The thicker trunk, the one nearest the path, the one by the bench">Couldn't tell which tree</button>
        <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="could not reach it" data-q="What stopped you? (optional)" data-ph="A locked gate, a fence, opening hours, private land">Couldn't reach it</button>
        <button type="button" class="worthit-chip" data-reason="something else" data-q="Tell us in a line." data-ph="What we got wrong, or what we are missing">Something else</button>
      </div>
      <span class="worthit-thanks" hidden>Thanks, we'll check it.</span>
      <form class="worthit-detail" hidden>
        <label class="worthit-q" for={`wd-${treeId}`}>Anything that helps us check? (optional)</label>
        <textarea id={`wd-${treeId}`} rows="2" placeholder=""></textarea>
        <button type="submit" class="worthit-chip">Send</button>
      </form>
    </Fragment>
  )}
</div>
